The Nautilus DevOps team is working on automating infrastructure deployment using AWS CloudFormation. 
As part of this effort, they need to create a CloudFormation stack that provisions an S3 bucket with versioning enabled.

Create a CloudFormation stack named xfusion-stack using Terraform. 
This stack should contain an S3 bucket named xfusion-bucket-547186510 as a resource, and the bucket must have versioning enabled. 
The Terraform working directory is /home/bob/terraform. Create the main.tf file (do not create a different .tf file) to accomplish this task.

Note: Right-click under the EXPLORER section in VS Code and select Open in Integrated Terminal to launch the terminal.

SOLUTION
Here is your /home/bob/terraform/main.tf to create the CloudFormation stack that provisions an S3 bucket with versioning enabled:

hcl
resource "aws_cloudformation_stack" "xfusion_stack" {
  name = "xfusion-stack"

  template_body = jsonencode({
    AWSTemplateFormatVersion = "2010-09-09"
    Resources = {
      XfusionBucket = {
        Type = "AWS::S3::Bucket"
        Properties = {
          BucketName = "xfusion-bucket-547186510"
          VersioningConfiguration = {
            Status = "Enabled"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  })
}
💡 Key Details
Stack Name: Exactly xfusion-stack as required.

Template Body: Inline JSON template using jsonencode() . The template_body argument supports up to 51,200 bytes, which is more than enough for this single-resource template .

S3 Bucket: Defined as an AWS::S3::Bucket resource with BucketName = "xfusion-bucket-547186510".

Versioning: Enabled via VersioningConfiguration with Status = "Enabled" . This is the required property to turn on S3 versioning through CloudFormation.

Region: Handled by your existing provider.tf (us-east-1).

🚀 Execution Steps
bash
cd /home/bob/terraform
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply --auto-approve
✅ Confirm No Changes
bash
terraform plan
It should return:

text
No changes. Your infrastructure matches the configuration.
🔍 Verify (optional)
bash
aws --endpoint-url=http://aws:4566 cloudformation describe-stacks --stack-name xfusion-stack
aws --endpoint-url=http://aws:4566 s3api get-bucket-versioning --bucket xfusion-bucket-547186510
The first command should show the stack status as CREATE_COMPLETE, and the second should return "Status": "Enabled", confirming versioning is active on the bucket.

